operty is state owned. Yes is indicated with either a 'true' or '1'. No is indicated with either a 'false' or '0'.\nNOTE: State owned property is land or other assets that are legally owned by  the state.","type":"boolean","sortOrder":62,"isSearchable":false,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"10a07318-0f7d-4b80-a58b-449f24407366","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"fe61d32585421c50639ba244992b0857f0fc52c2","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"disasterAssistanceCoverageRequiredCode","title":"Disaster Assistance Coverage Required Code","description":"Indicates which federal agency has required the purchase of flood insurance as a requirement for disaster assistance.\nLegal values (value : description):\n0 : Not Required;\n1 : SBA;\n2 : FEMA;\n4 : HHS (canceled, effective October 1, 2009);\n5 : Other Agency;","type":"smallint","sortOrder":63,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"8aab7143-7227-4637-acce-c615afde34a9","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"ce2fc8e3811f5fbc8523c8dfbc52baa8895e644c","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"mandatoryPurchaseFlag","title":"Mandatory Purchase Flag","description":"Indicates if the policy is required by the mortgage lender. Yes is indicated with either a 'true' or '1'. No is indicated with either a 'false' or '0'","type":"boolean","sortOrder":64,"isSearchable":false,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"78a47cc9-624b-4a22-9fb5-5300e0d432cb","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"36a5d97dcc809a574cf393277187ae0e790c909d","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"grandfatheringTypeCode","title":"Grandfathering Type Code","description":"Type of grandfathering, if applicable, in place for rating\nLegal values (value : description):\n1 : No Grandfathering;\n2 : Grandfathering Built to Code;\n3 : Grandfathering Continuous Coverage;\nNote: Grandfathering is a rating procedure that enables policyholders to use a prior food map for rating if the building was built in compliance or continuously insured","type":"smallint","sortOrder":65,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"014dc0e2-9875-45e7-ad34-93301dbd9a12","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"b556384c3bb7ba9f1820ed2dfd37d2720dd1371a","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"programTypeIndicator","title":"Program Type Indicator","description":"Indicates if a property is qualified for emergency program coverage (true) or regular coverage (false). Yes is indicated with either a 'true' or '1'. No is indicated with either a 'false' or '0'.\nNOTE: The initial phase of a communitys participation in the NFIP, as prescribed by Section 1306 of the National Flood Insurance Act of 1968 (NFIA) (42 U.S.C. 4056). In this phase, limited amounts of coverage are available.","type":"boolean","sortOrder":69,"isSearchable":false,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"550ba22c-979b-4b9b-bd79-6a918be6fbb5","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"8d1afe60388e12f163c635b0c53856e1aa7a9ed0","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"mapPanelNumber","title":"Map Panel Number","description":"Either the current map panel number for the property or the map panel number being used for rating, depending on MapInfo Type.","type":"text","sortOrder":70,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"3a7d5013-06b3-4262-af64-9ab72241eeb6","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"8e1c64aa5f31e8e73f4c921d36a998836f46ab22","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"mapPanelSuffix","title":"Map Panel Suffix","description":"Either the current map panel suffix for the property or the map panel suffix used for rating, depending on MapInfo Type.","type":"text","sortOrder":71,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"e33a5d0a-dce2-4790-a886-e06b7e978e25","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"78fe6aa21d393f68a65e66fc333d34cebf021b93","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"floodZoneCurrent","title":"Current Flood Zone","description":"Flood zone derived from the Flood Insurance Rate Map (FIRM) where the insured property is currently located.\n\nA - Special Flood with no Base Flood Elevation on FIRM; \nAE, A1-A30 - Special Flood with Base Flood Elevation on FIRM; \nA99 - Special Flood with Protection Zone; \nAH, AHB* - Special Flood with Shallow Ponding; \nAO, AOB* - Special Flood with Sheet Flow; \nX, B - Moderate Flood from primary water source.  Pockets of areas subject to drainage problems; \nX, C - Minimal Flood from primary water source.  Pockets of areas subject to drainage problems; \nD - Possible Flood; \nV - Velocity Flood with no Base Flood Elevation on FIRM; \nVE, V1-V30 - Velocity Flood with Base Flood Elevation on FIRM; \nAE, VE, X - New zone designations used on new maps starting January 1, 1986, in lieu of A1-A30, V1-V30, and B and C; \nAR - A Special Flood Hazard Area that results from the decertification of a previously accredited flood protection system that is determined to be in the process of being restored to provide base flood protection;\nAR Dual Zones - (AR/AE, AR/A1-A30, AR/AH, AR/AO, AR/A) Areas subject to flooding from failure of the flood protection system (Zone AR) which also overlap an existing Special Flood Hazard Area as a dual zone; \n\n*AHB, AOB, ARE, ARH, ARO, and ARA are not risk zones shown on a map, but are acceptable values for rating purposes","type":"text","sortOrder":72,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"0688d869-8272-4aaa-848a-c9c7e7c10fdf","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"a0e56d8cb323d349c3fac086f2884f747e09a5c7","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"femaRegion","title":"FEMA Region","description":"FEMA Region","type":"smallint","sortOrder":73,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"90615068-fe15-49ac-a184-a72f2cb23d84","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"043684543296da74ac320d64d8b1e2196a5187f5","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"propertyState","title":"Property State","description":"The two-character alpha abbreviation of the state in which the insured property is located","type":"text","sortOrder":74,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"1b8af072-a54b-4cb0-80f9-dd3f5f6e5920","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"4b47374cb6996ad87977985f2b6c6f62153cf34c","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"reportedZipCode","title":"Reported Zip Code","description":"5-digit Postal  Zip Code for the insured property reported by WYO partners","type":"text","sortOrder":76,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"96580e57-d884-41bd-a6b3-977263f5655e","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"46ab3f19105d92ca80764d1931083313ba08bdad","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"censusGeoid","title":"Census Block Group FIPS","description":"Numeric code that uniquely identifies all administrative/legal and statistical geographic areas for which the Census Bureau tabulates data. In this instance, the Census GeoID is presented at the Census Block Group level. This is an address-based 12-character code that is the concatenation of fields consisting of the 2-character state FIPS code, the 3-character county FIPS code, the 6-character census tract code, and the 1-character block group code. Block numbers beginning with a zero are associated with water-only areas. Please see: https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/geography/guidance/geo-identifiers.html","type":"text","sortOrder":77,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"5e489c3e-9338-4c49-8af7-c4dd202b0819","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"bd70f84ea48b4d4efaa27db9008066bea2a992b7","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"latitude","title":"Latitude","description":"Approximate latitude of the insured building (to 1 decimal place). This represents the approximate location of the insured property. The precision has been lessened to ensure individual privacy. This may result in a point location that exists in an incorrect county or state. Use the state and county fields for record aggregation for these dimensions","type":"decimal(9,1)","sortOrder":78,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"6447419b-2191-4908-bf08-e55900bbff84","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"cb6569adfc508265a161d2605c9b4eeed44057d1","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"longitude","title":"Longitude","description":"Approximate longitude of the insured building (to 1 decimal place). This represents the approximate location of the insured property. The precision has been lessened to ensure individual privacy. This may result in a point location that exists in an incorrect county or state. Use the state and county fields for record aggregation for these dimensions","type":"decimal(9,1)","sortOrder":79,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"18d07f12-937f-4b0a-b198-695c5969d978","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"0aefcf4b4800519eeffc6205e25fa83240adbfcd","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"buildingOnFederalLand","title":"Building on Federal Land Indicator","description":"An indicator of whether or not a building meets the NFIP definition of being located on federal land. Yes, is indicated with either a 'true' or '1'. No is indicated with either a 'false' or '0'","type":"boolean","sortOrder":80,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"699f7b26-4f21-4014-a87d-b84bdd451c45","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"71780d66a58cb5f403ee492b7d9d635617e6d63a","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"buildingPurpose","title":"Building Purpose","description":"Indicates if the building is residential, non-residential or mixed use.  (value : description): R : Residential (100%) N : Non-Residential (100%) M : Mixed Use","type":"text","sortOrder":81,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"1c78ecf6-4ff1-48df-a1d6-c16af504f181","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"5a33085e3986ca8a13c4b4f22ea613c74bde1bbc","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"seasonallyOccupied","title":"Seasonally Occupied Indicator","description":"An indicator of whether or not a building meets the NFIP definition of being seasonally occupied. Yes, is indicated with either a 'true' or '1'. No is indicated with either a 'false' or '0'","type":"boolean","sortOrder":82,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"aa990c85-302a-4fef-ae54-def8588a1b78","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"d1f6cb7f9049a802b905e8485a53929e442a783f","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"fullRiskPremium","title":"Full Risk Premium","description":"The chargeable premium for a property based on its determined flood risk and the full cost to pay anticipated losses and expenses for that property.","type":"integer","sortOrder":83,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"d934ad36-6fb9-4a13-b596-1acabfc1acd4","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"520be1e0727e430c3075df7527cae495d149aa94","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"buildingOverWaterType","title":"Building Over Water Type","description":"Indicates if the insured building is not over water, partially over water, or fully/entirely over water. 1 : Not over Water 2 : Partially over Water 3 : Fully/Entirely over Water","type":"smallint","sortOrder":84,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"37a981a6-877d-440e-8af8-f02e875514b1","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"8b4e355bf96cb42e9b26cdc10f8932dd5b111c4d","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"foundationType","title":"Foundation Type","description":"Type of foundation of the building or structure.\n1 - Slab\n2 - Basement \n3 - CrawlSpace \n4 - Elevated Without Enclosure Post Pile or Pier \n5 - Elevated With Enclosure Post Pile or Pier \n6 - Elevated With Enclosure Not Post Pile or Pier","type":"text","sortOrder":85,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"03a8f402-f192-4c99-8887-835d23711da1","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"403d360325862e15fe40fd25856730f7849677db","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"id","title":"ID","description":"Unique ID assigned to the record","type":"bigint","sortOrder":87,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":false,"primaryKey":true,"id":"86c95f69-cff9-4dea-8a30-f60cc308cd15","lastRefresh":"2026-07-21T03:00:15.883Z","hash":"0ea49d5d0e97e28049172eb7efe6408badb1e261","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"obstructionType","title":"Obstruction Type","description":"Code that describes the type of obstruction that may be present under an elevated building. An obstruction includes an enclosed area and/or machinery and equipment attached to the building below the lowest elevated floor.\n10 : Free of obstruction\n15 : With obstruction: enclosure/crawlspace with proper openings not used for rating (not applicable in V Zones)\n20 : With obstruction: less than 300 sq. ft. with breakaway walls, but no machinery or equipment attached to building below lowest elevated floor, or the elevation of the machinery or equipment is at or above the Base Flood Elevation\n24 : With obstruction: less than 300 sq. ft. with breakaway walls or finished enclosure and with machinery or equipment attached to building below lowest elevated floor. The elevation of the machinery or equipment is below the Base Flood Elevation.\n30 : With obstruction: 300 sq. ft. or more with breakaway walls, but no machinery or equipment attached to building below the Base Flood Elevation\n34 : With obstruction: 300 sq. ft. or more with breakaway walls or finished enclosure and with machinery or equipment attached to building below the Base Flood Elevation\n40 : With obstruction: no walls, but the elevation of machinery or equipment attached to building is below Base Flood Elevation\n50 : With obstruction: non-breakaway walls/crawlspace or finished enclosure with no machinery or equipment attached to building below lowest elevated floor\n54 : With obstruction: non-breakaway walls/crawlspace or finished enclosure with machinery or equipment attached to building below lowest elevated floor\n60 : With obstruction\n70 : With Certification subgrade crawlspace (AE, A01-A30, unnumbered A, AO, AH,AOB, AHB zones)\n80 : Without Certification subgrade crawlspace (all zones)\n90 : With Enclosure: Elevated buildings with elevator below the BFE in A zones. No other enclosure below the BFE.\n91 : Free of Obstruction: Elevated buildings with lattice, slats, or shutters (including louvers) enclosing the elevator below the BFE in V zones. No other obstruction or machinery and equipment (M&E) servicing the building located below the BFE. The building will be rated free of obstruction with the V zone elevator loading added to the building basic limit.\n92 : With Enclosure: Elevated buildings with elevator below the BFE in A zones. Enclosure below the BFE has no proper openings, is finished, or is used for other than parking, building access,or storage.\n94 : With Obstruction: Elevated buildings with elevator below the BFE in V zones. No other obstruction or machinery and equipment (M&E)servicing the building located belowthe BFE.\n95 : With Obstruction: Elevated buildings with elevator below the BFE in V zones. Breakaway wall obstruction is unfinished and elevator and obstruction are located below the BFE but no machinery and equipment (M&E) servicing the building is located below the BFE.\n96 : With Obstruction: Elevated buildings with elevator below the BFE in V zones. Breakaway wall obstruction is finished or is used for other than parking, building access, or storage.\n97 : With Obstruction: Elevated buildings with elevator below the BFE in V zones. No other obstruction, but has M&E servicing the building located below the BFE.\n98 : With Obstruction: Elevated buildings with elevator below the BFE in V zones. Breakaway walls obstruction and M&E servicing the building are located below the BFE.","type":"smallint","sortOrder":23,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"3f8e9d36-965e-480f-8162-9ea318fcc1fb","lastRefresh":"2026-07-23T22:40:51.366Z","hash":"4158dc7662674fb05fa0c6cc76cfe1bc6cf2a683","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"nfipRatedCommunityNumber","title":"Rated NFIP Community ID Number","description":"A six-digit designation identifying the rated NFIP community. The first two numbers are the state code. The next four are the FEMA-assigned community number. An alphabetical suffix is added to a community number to identify revisions in the FIRM for that community","type":"text","sortOrder":66,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"6e1d7476-785f-480e-a35f-6a99b891204b","lastRefresh":"2026-07-23T22:40:51.366Z","hash":"f4e4f9517c2c10a52099fd7848f8129bf6c43eaf","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"nfipCommunityNumberCurrent","title":"Current NFIP Community Number","description":"A six-digit designation identifying the current NFIP community. The first two numbers are the state code. The next four are the FEMA-assigned community number. An alphabetical suffix is added to a community number to identify revisions in the FIRM for that community","type":"text","sortOrder":67,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"866b2816-c299-4291-8381-dde6dc912f4b","lastRefresh":"2026-07-23T22:40:51.366Z","hash":"172d2aaea3467742892e0eba6b0a942660210b33","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"nfipCommunityName","title":"Rated NFIP Community Name","description":"A local political entity that has the authority to adopt and enforce floodplain ordinances for the area under its jurisdiction.","type":"text","sortOrder":68,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"165795f2-a4ec-40b8-843d-4c17ef42e277","lastRefresh":"2026-07-23T22:40:51.366Z","hash":"58d5e80c51b2f3c9b444b54fdf2259ccf3e9e7c3","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"reportedCity","title":"Reported City","description":"City where the insured building is located. A value of \"NA\" indicates the city value is currently unavailable.","type":"text","sortOrder":75,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"d7b124cb-1682-49f6-a729-46fdc555e4ff","lastRefresh":"2026-07-23T22:40:51.366Z","hash":"780153412ab73186efa7241f9c9be06efd6cc2e6","srid":null},{"datasetId":"openfema-96","openFemaDataSet":"NfipPolicies","datasetVersion":3,"name":"elevationDifference","title":"Elevation Difference","description":"Difference between the elevation of the lowest floor used for rating, or the floodproofed elevation, and the base flood elevation (BFE), or base flood depth, as appropriate. Round to nearest higher elevation difference in whole feet using .5 as the midpoint\n\nNOTE: The depth shown on the Flood Insurance Rate Map (FIRM) for Zone AO that indicates the depth of water above the highest adjacent grade resulting from a flood that has a 1% chance of equaling or exceeding that level in any given year. The elevation of surface water resulting from a flood that has a 1% chance of equaling or exceeding that level in any given year. The BFE is shown on the FloodInsurance Rate Map (FIRM) for Zones AE, AH, A1-A30, AR, AR/A, AR/AE, AR/A1-A30, AR/AH, AR/A0, V1-V30 andVE.\nThe value of 9999.0 indicates the field is not reported and/or used for this policy","type":"integer","sortOrder":13,"isSearchable":true,"isNestedObject":false,"isNullable":true,"primaryKey":false,"id":"77b15e59-f98b-40a7-8cdf-d51749ad7781","lastRefresh":"2026-08-04T22:40:37.348Z","hash":"527347495c188ad0a4f838b4cd3224a8229d1cb8","srid":null}]}
